# Retail Inventory Management Analysis 📊

## 📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing retail sales, inventory, product, and supplier data using **MySQL**.

The objective is to use SQL to analyze business performance, identify high-performing products, monitor inventory levels, evaluate suppliers, and generate useful business insights.

This project demonstrates practical SQL skills required for **Data Analyst** roles.

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

- MySQL
- MySQL Workbench
- SQL
- GitHub

---

## 🗄️ Database Structure

The project contains four main tables:

### 1. Suppliers

Stores information about product suppliers.

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| supplier_id | Unique supplier ID |
| supplier_name | Name of supplier |
| city | Supplier location |

### 2. Products

Stores product information.

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| product_id | Unique product ID |
| product_name | Product name |
| category | Product category |
| supplier_id | Supplier reference |
| unit_price | Price per unit |

### 3. Inventory

Stores current inventory information.

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| inventory_id | Unique inventory ID |
| product_id | Product reference |
| stock_quantity | Current stock |
| reorder_level | Minimum stock level |
| last_updated | Last inventory update date |

### 4. Sales

Stores sales transactions.

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| sale_id | Unique sale ID |
| product_id | Product reference |
| sale_date | Date of sale |
| quantity_sold | Units sold |
| sales_amount | Revenue generated |

